<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Name this def in a TileMutatorDef's <extraGenSteps> and the cast arrives with
    the map. MapGenerator.GenerateMap concatenates every active mutator's
    extraGenSteps into the step list before sorting by <order>, so no patch is
    needed anywhere.

    order 900 puts this after terrain, structures and scatterers – the company
    has to have somewhere to stand before it is placed.
  -->
  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>Inhabited_Cast</defName>
    <order>900</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.Inhabited.GenStep_InhabitedCast" />
  </GenStepDef>

  <!--
    INHABITED_STOCK_ONTO_MAP_AND_FATE_1: the place's larder and trade goods,
    put on the ground as real Things.

    order 910 runs it AFTER Inhabited_Cast (900) and that ordering is
    load-bearing, not tidiness: WorldObject_Inhabited.InstantiateCast is what
    fills the stock holder, and the cast step is what calls it. Dropping first
    would empty a holder that is still empty.

    ⚠️ ANY TileMutatorDef THAT NAMES Inhabited_Cast MUST NAME THIS TOO. The
    wilderness PLACE path reaches a GenStep only through a mutator's
    <extraGenSteps>; a mutator listing the cast and not the stock generates
    people with no goods, silently. The settlement path is wired in
    Inhabited_SettlementMapGenerator's genSteps list.

    RM_ prefix, unlike its Inhabited_* siblings: NEW defNames take the
    three-tier grammar in design/NAMING_SCHEME_PLAN.md (RimMandrake tier), and
    the older names migrate under NAMING_SCHEME_EXECUTION_1 rather than being
    renamed ahead of it.
  -->
  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>RM_InhabitedStock</defName>
    <order>910</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.Inhabited.GenStep_InhabitedStock" />
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
